---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { t, type Locale } from '../i18n';

interface Props { lang: Locale }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const s = t(lang);
---

<Base lang={lang} route="/about/" section="about" title={s.nav.about}>
  <article class="wrap about prose">
    {lang === 'zh' ? (
      <Fragment>
        <h1>关于 Gaiya Daily</h1>
        <p class="lede">每天 5 条 AI 新闻,写给自己做产品、自己卖的人。不管你写不写代码,读一遍就能懂。</p>
        <h2>每天怎么来的</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>程序从十几个地方收集前一天的 AI 新闻:Hacker News、GitHub 热门、Hugging Face 每日论文、Techmeme、各家 AI 公司的官方博客等。</li>
          <li>合并重复的报道,按"热度"和"对自己做产品的人有没有用"打分,选出 5 条。</li>
          <li>AI 读原文,把事实整理成一张卡片,每条事实都标出处。稿子只能用卡片上的事实来写。</li>
          <li>AI 起草中英文两个版本,再由程序检查有没有编造的说法、照搬原文、营销腔。</li>
          <li>作者本人逐条审过才发,有话要说就在"作者按"里写下自己的判断。</li>
        </ol>
        <p>每天美西时间早上 4 点(美东 7 点,北京时间晚上 7 到 8 点)上线。</p>
        <h2>谁在做</h2>
        <p><a href="https://gaiya.cc">Gaiya Lab</a> 是一个人的应用工作室,在 iOS、Android、macOS、Windows 上做过十个小应用。另一个项目 <a href="https://teardown.gaiya.cc">Teardown</a> 拆解独立产品是怎么做起来的。</p>
        <h2>说清楚的几件事</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>写稿用了 AI。事实以原文为准,每条都附来源链接,欢迎点进去核对。</li>
          <li>"据称""某公司说"的地方,是我们没法独立验证的说法。</li>
          <li>发现错误请在 X 上找 <a href="https://x.com/gaiya_l">@gaiya_l</a>,改正后会在原文注明。</li>
        </ul>
      </Fragment>
    ) : (
      <Fragment>
        <h1>About Gaiya Daily</h1>
        <p class="lede">Five AI stories a day for people who make and sell their own products. You don't need to write code to follow along.</p>
        <h2>How each issue is made</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A script collects the previous day's AI news from more than a dozen places: Hacker News, GitHub Trending, Hugging Face Daily Papers, Techmeme, and the official blogs of the AI companies.</li>
          <li>Duplicate stories are merged, and each one is scored on how much attention it's getting and how useful it is to someone shipping their own product. The top five make the issue.</li>
          <li>AI reads the original sources and writes down the facts, each with where it came from. The drafts may only use those facts.</li>
          <li>AI drafts the English and Chinese versions. Automated checks look for claims the sources don't support, copied sentences and marketing language.</li>
          <li>The maker reviews every item before it goes out, and adds a Maker's note when they have something of their own to say.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>New issues go up at 4am Pacific, 7am Eastern.</p>
        <h2>Who makes it</h2>
        <p><a href="https://gaiya.cc">Gaiya Lab</a> is a one-person studio that has shipped ten small apps on iOS, Android, macOS and Windows. Its other project, <a href="https://teardown.gaiya.cc">Teardown</a>, takes indie products apart to see how they work.</p>
        <h2>Ground rules</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>AI helps write this. The sources are the authority, and every item links to them so you can check.</li>
          <li>When we write "says" or "claims", it's something we couldn't verify ourselves.</li>
          <li>Spotted a mistake? Tell <a href="https://x.com/gaiya_l">@gaiya_l</a> on X. Corrections are noted on the page.</li>
        </ul>
      </Fragment>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 44rem; padding-top: var(--stack); }
  .lede { margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
